# Implemented

RuntimeCompactionBinding persists launch runtime, explicit session id, common
random epoch and exact validated native transcript path in private atomic JSON
under ROUTER_INSTANCE_DIR. Launcher and router processes use the same record.
No arbitrary workspace-latest fallback: a missing exact id remains unbound.
ChannelTranscriptRepository performs scoped selection; native metadata must
match the requested id. New epochs invalidate earlier controller proof.

The facade passes this binding into pending IO, terminal policy, desktop channel
ports, and Claude/OpenAI request and failure callbacks. Raw request callbacks
precede channel-body append in the concurrently updated router support modules.
HTTP observations reject mismatched session ids and Claude agent-id requests.
Missing HTTP identity cannot prove pressure or shrink. Trusted in-process
observations use headers=None.

# Pressure and checkpoint proof

Input budget mirrors the request builder: context capacity minus configured
ratio-capped output reserve minus context guard reserve, with its 8192 floor.
A bounded 512 KiB native tail seeds resumed-session pressure before external
submission: Claude input+cache read+cache creation, Codex last_token_usage input
(not cumulative usage). Unknown remains unknown. A newer checkpoint invalidates
older usage; initial seed never supplies shrink proof. A first real request
prevents another process from re-seeding stale tail usage.

Native compact/checkpoint alone does not mark verified. After a persisted
checkpoint the consumer gate permits a probe to cause the real next native
request; router append remains paused until raw request shrink is observed.
A non-shrinking request keeps admission paused and controller bounded retry is
preserved. Direct Anthropic native pressure and remote bridge ownership bypass
are preserved; explicitly observed native compaction can still finish proof.

